# Plugin System

## Architecture

```
shared/lib/plugins/
├── types.ts      ← PluginManifest, Plugin, PluginAPI, SlotName, Permissions
├── registry.ts   ← registration, lifecycle (activate/deactivate), slot contributions, events
├── api.ts        ← PluginAPI factory (restricted surface for each plugin)
└── setup.ts      ← bootstrap (main-app.tsx), window.__plugins__ dev tool
```

## Concept

Plugins extend the application through **slots** (extension points) — named points in UI and logic where a plugin can add:
- **Visual contributions** (`render`) — React components
- **Action contributions** (`handler`) — action handlers

Each plugin:
1. Declares a `PluginManifest` (id, name, version, permissions, slots)
2. Implements `activate(api)` — receives a restricted `PluginAPI`
3. Registers contributions into slots via the API

## Slots (Extension Points)

| Slot | Type | Location in UI |
|------|------|----------------|
| `sidebar:widget` | visual | Widgets at the bottom of the sidebar |
| `sidebar:footer` | visual | Sidebar footer |
| `topbar:action` | visual | Buttons in the top bar |
| `message:action` | action | Actions in the message context menu |
| `message:renderer` | visual | Message renderers (cards, previews) |
| `composer:toolbar` | visual | Buttons in the composer toolbar |
| `composer:slash-command` | action | Slash commands (/summarize, /translate) |
| `settings:panel` | visual | Sections in settings |
| `route:custom` | visual | Custom pages |

## Example: Creating a Plugin

```ts
import type { Plugin } from "~/shared/lib/plugins";

const myPlugin: Plugin = {
  manifest: {
    id: "com.example.translate",
    name: "Auto Translate",
    version: "1.0.0",
    description: "Translates messages on the fly",
    permissions: ["read:messages", "analytics", "storage"],
    slots: ["message:action", "composer:slash-command"],
  },

  activate(api) {
    api.log.info("Translate plugin activated");

    // Add action to the message context menu
    api.contribute({
      slot: "message:action",
      label: "Translate",
      icon: "translate",
      priority: 50,
      handler: async (message) => {
        const translated = await translateText(message.content);
        api.log.info("Translated", { messageId: message.id });
        api.track?.("message_translated", { from: "ru", to: "en" });
      },
    });

    // Slash command /translate
    api.contribute({
      slot: "composer:slash-command",
      label: "/translate",
      handler: async (context) => {
        // context.text — text after the command
      },
    });
  },

  deactivate() {
    // Cleanup (contributions are removed automatically)
  },
};

export default myPlugin;
```

## Plugin Registration

### Built-in (in application code)

```ts
// In setup.ts or main.tsx
import { registerPlugin } from "~/shared/lib/plugins";
import translatePlugin from "./plugins/translate";

registerPlugin(translatePlugin);
```

### Dynamic (external script)

```ts
// From <script> tag or dynamic import
import { loadPlugin } from "~/shared/lib/plugins/setup";

loadPlugin({
  manifest: { id: "com.ext.widget", name: "Widget", version: "1.0.0" },
  activate(api) { /* ... */ },
});
```

### Via dev console

```js
window.__plugins__.register({
  manifest: { id: "dev.test", name: "Test", version: "0.1.0" },
  activate(api) { api.log.info("Hello from dev plugin"); },
});
window.__plugins__.activate("dev.test");
```

## Using Slots in Components

### Visual slot

```tsx
import { PluginSlot } from "~/shared/lib/plugins";

function SidebarFooter() {
  return (
    <div>
      {/* Built-in UI */}
      <PluginSlot name="sidebar:footer" className="mt-2 space-y-1" />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Actions (message actions, slash commands)

```tsx
import { useSlotActions } from "~/shared/lib/plugins";

function MessageContextMenu({ message }) {
  const pluginActions = useSlotActions("message:action", message);

  return (
    <menu>
      {/* Built-in actions */}
      <li onClick={handleReply}>Reply</li>

      {/* Plugin actions */}
      {pluginActions.map(action => (
        <li key={action.pluginId} onClick={action.execute}>
          {action.label}
        </li>
      ))}
    </menu>
  );
}
```

## PluginAPI (Restricted Surface)

| Method | Description | Requires permission |
|--------|-------------|---------------------|
| `contribute()` | Register into a slot | — |
| `removeContributions()` | Remove own contributions | — |
| `navigate(path)` | Route navigation | `navigate` |
| `storage.get/set/remove` | Scoped localStorage | `storage` |
| `log.*` | Logging (scoped) | — |
| `data.getCurrentUserId()` | Current user ID | — |
| `data.getStreams()` | Channel list | `read:streams` |
| `data.getUnreadCount()` | Unread count | `read:messages` |
| `data.getTheme()` | Current theme | — |
| `data.getLocale()` | Current locale | — |
| `data.getRuntime()` | web/pwa/electron | — |
| `track(event, props)` | Analytics | `analytics` |
| `notify(title, body)` | Notifications | `notifications` |
| `on(event, handler)` | Event subscription | — |

## Permissions

```ts
type PluginPermission =
  | "read:messages"    // access to messages (metadata)
  | "read:users"       // access to user list
  | "read:streams"     // access to channels
  | "read:settings"    // access to settings
  | "write:messages"   // send messages
  | "navigate"         // route navigation
  | "notifications"    // show notifications
  | "analytics"        // send analytics
  | "shortcuts"        // register keyboard shortcuts
  | "storage";         // localStorage (scoped)
```

## Events (for plugin subscriptions)

| Event | Data |
|-------|------|
| `message:received` | `{ id, streamId, senderId, timestamp }` |
| `message:sent` | `{ id, streamId }` |
| `navigation:changed` | `{ path, params }` |
| `theme:changed` | `{ mode, palette }` |
| `network:status` | `{ online }` |
| `plugin:activated` | `{ pluginId }` |
| `plugin:deactivated` | `{ pluginId }` |

Host code emits events:
```ts
import { emitEvent } from "~/shared/lib/plugins";

emitEvent("message:received", { id: 123, streamId: 10 });
```

## Rules for AI Agent

### When adding a new extension point

1. Add `SlotName` to `types.ts`
2. Add `<PluginSlot name="..."/>` or `useSlotActions("...")` in the component
3. Document in the slots table above
4. Describe the `context` (props) format passed to contributions

### When implementing a feature

1. **Check `useSlotActions()`** — in context menus and action bars, always render plugin actions after built-in ones
2. **Don't break plugins** — when refactoring slots, maintain backward compatibility of SlotName
3. **Emit events** — on key user actions, call `emitEvent()` so plugins can react

### When creating a plugin

1. **Minimum permissions** — only request what you need
2. **Cleanup in deactivate()** — release resources (timers, subscriptions). Contributions are removed automatically
3. **Don't access the DOM directly** — only via `contribute()` with a `render` function
4. **Don't import stores directly** — use `api.data.*`
5. **Version properly** — use semver in manifest

### Security

- Plugins DO NOT have direct `localStorage` access — only scoped via `api.storage`
- Plugins DO NOT have access to auth credentials
- All API calls are proxied through a permission check
- `contribute({ render })` renders inside a `data-plugin-slot` container — host-level ErrorBoundary protects against crashes
